TokenWorks application-maintained resource-bound patch for werift 0.27.0.
This is not an upstream werift API or an upstream resource-safety claim.
Source: https://github.com/shinyoshiaki/werift-webrtc/tree/v0.27.0
License source: https://raw.githubusercontent.com/shinyoshiaki/werift-webrtc/v0.27.0/LICENSE

The adjacent script and manifest retain exact original/patched SHA-256 digests
for the Node ESM bundle, CJS runtime modules and public transport declarations.
The patch adds bounded SCTP receive/send tasks, retransmission/reassembly and
SACK metadata accounting, DTLS handshake tasks/fragments/transcript reservations,
ICE early-check/checklist limits and real UDP send-callback consumption. It also
removes automatic UDP-to-TCP TURN fallback, makes PeerConnection.close singleflight,
and drains in-flight ICE gathering and SCTP/DTLS tasks before releasing PC credits.
It does not replace protocol parsers, cryptography, or native application RPC semantics.
Other werift entry points (polyfill/nonstandard) are not used by this carrier and
are not advertised as patched. Preserve werift's shipped third-party notices.

